{"abstract":"Bahr and Hutton recently developed an approach to compiler calculation that allows a wide range of compilers to be derived from specifications of their correctness. However, a limitation of the approach is that it results in compilers that produce tree-structured code. By contrast, realistic compilers produce code that is essentially graph-structured, where the edges in the graph represent jumps that transfer the flow of control to other locations in the code. In this article, we show how their approach can naturally be adapted to calculate compilers that produce graph-structured code, without changing the underlying calculational methodology, by using a higher-order abstract syntax representation of graphs.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Hutton, Graham"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798523"],"event":{"acronym":"ICFP","title":"ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Functional Programming"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Graphs","program calculation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond trees calculating graph based compilers functional pearl","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3674638","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798523","identifier":[{"id":"85201688438","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1a301061-af0b-4827-87e1-c4029c77b934"],"keyword":["graphs","higher-order abstract syntax","program calculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8AF0FFD321A1BE2533D72B1D5182F69B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3674638","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108631256/graphcalc-paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"huttonpau","last":"Hutton","name":"Hutton, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3674638","issn":["24751421"],"issue":"ICFP249","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"370-394","paperid":"249","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201688438"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1a301061-af0b-4827-87e1-c4029c77b934"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beyond Trees: Calculating Graph-Based Compilers (Functional Pearl)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798523","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The implementation of asynchronous systems, in particular graphical user interfaces, is traditionally based on an imperative model that uses shared mutable state and callbacks. While efficient, the combination of shared mutable state and callbacks is notoriously difficult to reason about and prone to errors. Functional reactive programming (FRP) provides an elegant alternative and recent theoretical advances in modal FRP suggest that it can be efficient as well. In this paper, we present Async Rattus, an FRP language embedded in Haskell. The distinguishing feature of Async Rattus is a modal type constructor that enables the composition of asynchronous subsystems by keeping track of each subsystem’s clock at compile time which in turn enables dynamically changing clocks at runtime. The central component of our implementation is a Haskell compiler plugin that, among other aspects, checks the stricter typing rules of Async Rattus and infers compile-time clocks. This is the first implementation of an asynchronous modal FRP language. By embedding the language in Haskell we can exploit the existing language and library ecosystem as well as rapidly experiment with new language features and library design. We hope that such experimentation with Async Rattus sparks further research in modal FRP and its applications.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Houlborg, Emil","Rørdam, Gregers Thomas Skat"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798536"],"event":{"acronym":"PADL","title":"International Symposium on Practical Aspects of Declarative Languages"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Functional Reactive Programming","Haskell","Modal Types","Type systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"asynchronous reactive programming with modal types in haskell","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108631212/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798536","identifier":[{"id":"85182603045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-67f49495-d2dc-481e-b7e0-ae551bc091be"],"keyword":["Functional Reactive Programming","Haskell","Modal Types","Type Systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6843DF08E9CB166A01C70944FED6B5CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108631212/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, MSc in Software Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"houlborgpau","last":"Houlborg","name":"Houlborg, Emil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregers Thomas Skat","key":"rørdampau","last":"Rørdam","name":"Rørdam, Gregers Thomas Skat","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-52038-9_2","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"18-36","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Practical Aspects of Declarative Languages","volume":"14512"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182603045"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-67f49495-d2dc-481e-b7e0-ae551bc091be"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Asynchronous Reactive Programming with Modal Types in Haskell","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798536","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Much work in the area of compiler calculation has focused on pure languages. While this simplifies the reasoning, it reduces the applicability. In this article, we show how an existing compiler calculation methodology can be naturally extended to languages with side effects. We achieve this by exploiting an algebraic approach to effects, which keeps the reasoning simple and provides flexibility in how effects are interpreted. To make the ideas accessible we only use elementary functional programming techniques.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Garby, Zac","Hutton, Graham","Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798534"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Algebraic Effects","Monads","program calculation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calculating compilers effectively functional pearl","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108631238/effcalc-paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798534","identifier":[{"id":"85203875435","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6327f4e1-ade7-494c-a3eb-2dce8efc095c"],"keyword":["algebraic effects","monads","program calculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E75B8DBE6CA1EAB8132D35AD3007AFE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108631238/effcalc-paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zac","key":"garbypau","last":"Garby","name":"Garby, Zac","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"huttonpau","last":"Hutton","name":"Hutton, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677999.3678283","pages":"109-119","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th ACM SIGPLAN International Haskell Symposium"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203875435"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6327f4e1-ade7-494c-a3eb-2dce8efc095c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Calculating Compilers Effectively (Functional Pearl)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798534","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
