{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240402"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-23","place":"Reykjavik, is","start":"2017-06-20","title":"32nd Annual ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science, LICS 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the clocks are ticking no more delays","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85034057414","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240402","identifier":[{"id":"85034057414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c2aa5deb-956f-4d2c-ba03-df5534010dd3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-630D39E9BE1A1DA679D15C607A02073F"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","locid":"e8539989-3da2-47ac-b2b4-ed449ec6c230","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lics.2017.8005097","eisbn":["9781509030187"],"issn":["10436871"],"issue":"32","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"2017 32nd Annual ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science, LICS 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034057414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2aa5deb-956f-4d2c-ba03-df5534010dd3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The clocks are ticking : No more delays!","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240402","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Guarded recursion in the sense of Nakano allows general recursive types and terms to be added to type theory without breaking consistency. Recent work has demonstrated applications of guarded recursion such as programming with codata, reasoning about coinductive types, as well as constructing and reasoning about denotational models of general recursive types. Guarded recursion can also be used as an abstract form of step-indexing for reasoning about programming languages with advanced features. Ultimately, we would like to have an implementation of a type theory with guarded recursion in which all these applications can be carried out and machine-checked. In this paper, we take a step towards this goal by devising a suitable reduction semantics. We present Clocked Type Theory, a new type theory for guarded recursion that is more suitable for reduction semantics than the existing ones. We prove confluence, strong normalisation and canonicity for its reduction semantics, constructing the theoretical basis for a future implementation. We show how coinductive types as exemplified by streams can be encoded, and derive that the type system ensures productivity of stream definitions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382138"],"event":{"acronym":"LICS","title":"ACM/IEEE Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["type theory guarded recursion reduction semantics strong normalisation coinductive types recursive types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the clocks are ticking no more delays reduction semantics for type theory with guarded recursion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82163359/bahr17lics_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382138","identifier":[{"id":"85034057414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3b6b9080-03bc-42d1-aac5-d6ae5413e329"],"keyword":["type theory, guarded recursion, reduction semantics, strong normalisation, coinductive types, recursive types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-630D39E9BE1A1DA679D15C607A02073F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82163359/bahr17lics_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans Bugge","key":"grathwohlpau","last":"Grathwohl","name":"Grathwohl, Hans Bugge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Ejlers","key":"møgelbergpau","last":"Møgelberg","locid":"10003d22-a201-4b64-88e3-b423bc76fcc2","name":"Møgelberg, Rasmus Ejlers","orcid":"0000-0003-0386-4376","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lics.2017.8005097","issn":["10436871"],"journal":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Annual Symposium on Logic in Computer Science"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034057414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3b6b9080-03bc-42d1-aac5-d6ae5413e329"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Clocks Are Ticking: No More Delays! : Reduction Semantics for Type Theory with Guarded Recursion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382138","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The confluence properties of lambda calculus and orthogonal term rewriting do not generalise to the corresponding infinitary calculi. In order to recover the confluence property in a meaningful way, Kennaway et al. introduced Böhm reduction, which extends the ordinary reduction relation so that `meaningless terms' can be contracted to a fresh constant ⊥. In previous work, we have established that Böhm reduction can be instead characterised by a different mode of convergences of transfinite reductions that is based on a partial order structure instead of a metric space. In this paper, we develop a corresponding theory of Böhm reduction for term graphs. Our main result is that partial order convergence in a term graph rewriting system can be truthfully and faithfully simulated by metric convergence in the Böhm extension of the system. To prove this result we generalise the notion of residuals and projections to the setting of infinitary term graph rewriting. As ancillary results we prove the infinitary strip lemma and the compression property, both for partial order and metric convergence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382926"],"event":{"acronym":"FSCD","title":"International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["term graphs confluence infinitary rewriting graph rewriting Böhm trees"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"böhm reduction in infinitary term graph rewriting systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2017.8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382926","identifier":[{"id":"85030541143","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6f4b4499-b1df-402c-b962-1ab0ba9a4d1d"],"keyword":["term graphs, confluence, infinitary rewriting, graph rewriting, Böhm trees"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-24D1FD5374817EFB99E0ABC70EB99590"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2017.8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2017/7712/pdf/LIPIcs-FSCD-2017-0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2017/7727","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82503489/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dale","key":"millerpedh","last":"Miller","name":"Miller, Dale","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.fscd.2017.8","eisbn":["9783959770477"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","subtitle":"FSCD 2017, September 3–9, 2017, Oxford, UK","title":"2nd International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction","volume":"84"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030541143"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6f4b4499-b1df-402c-b962-1ab0ba9a4d1d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Böhm Reduction in Infinitary Term Graph Rewriting Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382926","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We present a recursion scheme based on attribute grammars that can be transparently applied to trees and acyclic graphs. Our recursion scheme allows the programmer to implement a tree traversal or a tree transformation and then apply it to compact graph representations of trees instead. The resulting graph traversal or graph transformation avoids recomputation of intermediate results for shared nodes – even if intermediate results are used in different contexts. Consequently, this approach leads to asymptotic speedup proportional to the compression provided by the graph representation. In general, however, this sharing of intermediate results is not sound. Therefore, we complement our implementation of the recursion scheme with a number of correspondence theorems that ensure soundness for various classes of traversals. We illustrate the practical applicability of the implementation as well as the complementing theory with a number of examples.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Axelsson, Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384778"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology"],"keyword":["Attribute grammars","Directed acyclic graphs","Graph transformation","Sharing","graph traversal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generalising tree traversals and tree transformations to dags exploiting sharing without the pain","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81995915/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384778","identifier":[{"id":"84962109549","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ee519b3e-1814-4e48-bcf2-aca21453000d"],"keyword":["Attribute grammars","directed acyclic graphs","graph transformation","graph traversal","sharing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8EACFB8690A622F004D1EAE73FC913D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81995915/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"axelssonpau","last":"Axelsson","name":"Axelsson, Emil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scico.2016.03.006","issn":["01676423","18727964"],"issn_org":["01676423"],"journal":"Science of Computer Programming","pages":"63-97","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Science of Computer Programming","volume":"137"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962109549"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ee519b3e-1814-4e48-bcf2-aca21453000d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Generalising tree traversals and tree transformations to DAGs : Exploiting sharing without the pain","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384778","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In the field of program transformation, one often transforms programs into continuation-passing style to make their flow of control explicit, and then immediately removes the resulting continuations using defunctionalisation to make the programs first-order. In this article, we show how these two transformations can be fused together into a single transformation step that cuts out the need to first introduce and then eliminate continuations. Our approach is calculational, uses standard equational reasoning techniques, and is widely applicable.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Hutton, Graham"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381499"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Continuation passing style","Defunctionalisation","Equational Reasoning","Program transformation","first order programs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cutting out continuations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84973912580","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381499","identifier":[{"id":"84973912580","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0fc840ce-68a2-438e-9a59-670872afeed1"],"keyword":["continuation-passing style","defunctionalisation","equational reasoning","first-order programs","program transformation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC40DD46EED3CD3C941C1D6572C22C8F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"huttonpau","last":"Hutton","name":"Hutton, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-30936-1_10","eisbn":["9783319309361"],"isbn":["9783319309354"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"187-200","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Essays Dedicated to Philip Wadler on the Occasion of His 60th Birthday","title":"A List of Successes That Can Change the World","volume":"9600"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84973912580"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0fc840ce-68a2-438e-9a59-670872afeed1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cutting Out Continuations","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381499","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
