{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-537685"],"event":{"end":"2014-08-31","place":"Gothenburg, se","start":"2014-08-31","title":"ACM SIGPLAN Workshop on Generic Programming","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["closed type families expression problem modularity two level types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"composing and decomposing data types a closed type families implementation of data types à la carte","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-537685","identifier":[{"id":"84907403377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f1c450a0-3b6f-4707-931f-08f9bcec9824"],"keyword":["closed type families, expression problem, modularity, two-level types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-4BB696B40F066479731A13981526AB3D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2633628.2633635","isbn":["9781450330428"],"pages":"71-82","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 10th ACM SIGPLAN Workshop on Generic Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907403377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f1c450a0-3b6f-4707-931f-08f9bcec9824"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Composing and decomposing data types : a closed type families implementation of data types à la carte","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-537685","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The process-oriented event-driven transaction systems (POETS) architecture introduced by Henglein et al. is a novel software architecture for enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems. POETS employs a pragmatic separation between (i) transactional data, that is, what has happened; (ii) reports, that is, what can be derived from the transactional data; and (iii) contracts, that is, which transactions are expected in the future. Moreover, POETS applies domain-specific languages (DSLs) for specifying reports and contracts, in order to enable succinct declarative specifications as well as rapid adaptability and customisation. In this paper we present an implementation of a generalised and extended variant of the POETS architecture. The extensions amount to a customisable data model based on nominal subtyping; support for run-time changes to the data model, reports and contracts, while retaining full auditability; and support for referable data that may evolve over time, also while retaining full auditability as well as referential integrity. Besides the revised architecture, we present the DSLs used to specify data definitions, reports, and contracts respectively. Finally, we illustrate a use case scenario, which we implemented in a trial for a small business.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Jesper","Bahr, Patrick","Henglein, Fritz","Hvitved, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384657"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Auditability","Domain specific languages","Enterprise Resource Planning","POETS architecture","transactional data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"domain specific languages for enterprise systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-45234-9_6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384657","identifier":[{"id":"84910641672","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e5f0c10a-93f9-4b60-a946-5423a5be8422"],"keyword":["POETS architecture","auditability","domain-specific languages","enterprise resource planning","transactional data"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-2742ACCE342DAADDE09C6E92C110925B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-45234-9_6","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fritz","key":"hengleinpau","last":"Henglein","name":"Henglein, Fritz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"hvitvedpau","last":"Hvitved","name":"Hvitved, Tom","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","fir