{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521717"],"event":{"acronym":"FLOPS","end":"2014-06-06","place":"Kanazawa, jp","start":"2014-06-04","title":"International Symposium, FLOPS 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proving correctness of compilers using structured graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-521717","identifier":[{"id":"84902449585","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d6ad361b-b8f5-4ca8-bf5f-cb13299491c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-3B5F011607601D84FF51FE472FF002BF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-07151-0_14","eisbn":["9783319071510"],"isbn":["9783319071503"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"221-237","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"12th International Symposium, FLOPS 2014, Kanazawa, Japan, June 4-6, 2014. Proceedings","title":"Functional and logic programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902449585"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d6ad361b-b8f5-4ca8-bf5f-cb13299491c8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proving correctness of compilers using structured graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521717","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We present a modular framework for implementing languages with effects and control structures such as loops and conditionals. This framework enables modular definitions of both syntax and semantics as well as modular implementations of compilers and virtual machines. In order to compile control structures, in particular cyclic ones, we employ Oliveira and Cook's purely functional representation of graphs. Moreover, to separate control flow features semantically from other language features, we represent source languages using Johann and Ghani's encoding of generalised algebraic datatypes as fixpoints of higher-order functors. We demonstrate the usage of our modular compiler framework with an extended running example and highlight the extensibility of our modular compiler implementations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Day, Laurence E.","Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383418"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["modularity extensibility compiler virtual machine semantics catamorphism graph sharing Haskell"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pick n fix capturing control flow in modular compilers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383418","ids":["itu-92660987-7562-4246-8442-de39317de10e"],"keyword":["modularity, extensibility, compiler, virtual machine, semantics, catamorphism, graph, sharing, Haskell"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6FD83F63ED4199041D3B636DCD766969"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurence E.","key":"daypau","last":"Day","name":"Day, Laurence E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"TFP '14 pre-proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-92660987-7562-4246-8442-de39317de10e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pick'n'Fix: Capturing Control Flow in Modular Compilers","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383418","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We present an approach to compiler implementation using Oliveira and Cook’s structured graphs that avoids the use of explicit jumps in the generated code. The advantage of our method is that it takes the implementation of a compiler using a tree type along with its correctness proof and turns it into a compiler implementation using a graph type along with a correctness proof. The implementation and correctness proof of a compiler using a tree type without explicit jumps is simple, but yields code duplication. Our method provides a convenient way of improving such a compiler without giving up the benefits of simple reasoning.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383526"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["compiler verification graphs fold free monad"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proving correctness of compilers using structured graphs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-07151-0_14","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383526","identifier":[{"id":"84902449585","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9a5eeee0-4cba-4f56-91a2-0419d4aa4904"],"keyword":["compiler,verification,graphs,fold,free monad"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-3B5F011607601D84FF51FE472FF002BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-07151-0_14","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"codishpedh","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eijiro","key":"sumiipedh","last":"Sumii","name":"Sumii, Eijiro","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-07151-0_14","isbn":["9783319071503"],"pages":"221-237","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Functional and Logic Programming","volume":"8475"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902449585"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9a5eeee0-4cba-4f56-91a2-0419d4aa4904"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proving Correctness of Compilers Using Structured Graphs","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383526","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Banks and financial institutions nowadays often use domain-specific languages (DSLs) for describing complex financial contracts, in particular, for specifying how asset transfers for a specific contract depend on underlying observables, such as interest rates, currency rates, and stock prices. The seminal work by Peyton-Jones and Eber on financial contracts shows how an algebraic approach to contract specification can be used for valuation of contracts (when combined with a model of the underlying observables) and for managing how contracts evolve under so-called fixings and decision-taking, with the contracts eventually evaporating into the empty contract, for which no party have further obligations. The ideas have emerged into Eber's company LexiFi, which has become a leading software provider for a range of financial institutions, with all contract management operations centralised around a domain-specific contract language hosted in MLFi, a derivative of the functional programming language OCaml. In this paper, we present a small simple contract language, which rigorously relegates any artefacts of modelling and computation from its core. The language shares the same vision as the previously mentioned work with the addition that it (a) allows for specifying multi-party contracts (such as entire portfolios), (b) has good algebraic properties, well suited for formal reasoning, and yet (c) allows for expressing many interesting contracts appearing in real-world portfolios, such as various variations of so-called barrier options. We show that plenty of information can be derived from, and useful manipulations defined on, just the symbolic contract specification, independent of any stochastic aspects of the modelled contracts. Contracts modelled in our language are analysed and transformed for management according to a precise cash-flow semantics, modelled and checked using the Coq proof assistant. Implementations of the contract language in Haskell and Coq are available online together with machine-checkable proofs (in Coq) of the key properties of the contract language.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Berthold, Jost","Elsman, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383296"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["financial contracts multi party contracts formal verification Haskell Coq"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards certified management of financial contracts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383296","ids":["itu-8ab32989-c014-4484-978d-36ba40c164dc"],"keyword":["financial contracts, multi-party contracts, formal verification, Haskell, Coq"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-938B47780045D1E916408151C29EFFF3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jost","key":"bertholdpau","last":"Berthold","name":"Berthold, Jost","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"elsmanpau","last":"Elsman","name":"Elsman, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 26th Nordic Workshop on Programming Theory, NWPT '14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8ab32989-c014-4484-978d-36ba40c164dc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Certified Management of Financial Contracts","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383296","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Parent-teacher cross-informant agreement, although usually modest, may provide important clinical information. Using data for 27,962 children from 21 societies, we asked the following: (a) Do parents report more problems than teachers, and does this vary by society, age, gender, or type of problem? (b) Does parent-teacher agreement vary across different problem scales or across societies? (c) How well do parents and teachers in different societies agree on problem item ratings? (d) How much do parent-teacher dyads in different societies vary in within-dyad agreement on problem items? (e) How well do parents and teachers in 21 societies agree on whether the child's problem level exceeds a deviance threshold? We used five methods to test agreement for Child Behavior Checklist (CBCL) and Teacher's Report Form (TRF) ratings. CBCL scores were higher than TRF scores on most scales, but the informant differences varied in magnitude across the societies studied. Cross-informant correlations for problem scale scores varied moderately across societies studied and were significantly higher for Externalizing than Internalizing problems. Parents and teachers tended to rate the same items as low, medium, or high, but within-dyad item agreement varied widely in every society studied. In all societies studied, both parental noncorroboration of teacher-reported deviance and teacher noncorroboration of parent-reported deviance were common. Our findings underscore the importance of obtaining information from parents and teachers when evaluating and treating children, highlight the need to use multiple methods of quantifying cross-informant agreement, and provide comprehensive baselines for patterns of parent-teacher agreement across 21 societies.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Rescorla, Leslie A","Bochicchio, Lauren","Achenbach, Thomas M","Ivanova, Masha Y","Almqvist, Fredrik","Begovac, Ivan","Bilenberg, Niels","Bird, Hector","Dobrean, Anca","Erol, Nese","Fombonne, Eric","Fonseca, Antonio","Frigerio, Alessandra","Fung, Daniel S S","Lambert, Michael C","Leung, Patrick W L","Liu, Xianchen","Marković, Ivica","Markovic, Jasminka","Minaei, Asghar","Ooi, Yoon Phaik","Roussos, Alexandra","Rudan, Vlasta","Simsek, Zeynep","van der Ende, Jan","Weintraub, Sheila","Wolanczyk, Tomasz","Woo, Bernardine","Weiss, Bahr","Weisz, John","Zukauskiene, Rita","Verhulst, Frank C"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598335"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bryn Mawr College"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Child Behavior Disorders","Cross Cultural Comparison","Faculty","Female","Humans","Male","Observer Variation","Parents","Reproducibility of Results"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parent teacher agreement on children s problems in 000000000021 societies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15374416.2014.900719","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-598335","identifier":[{"id":"24787452","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84904389186","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-57bf5e79-5e0b-4206-bc12-515ae913f787"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Child","Child Behavior Disorders","Cross-Cultural Comparison","Faculty","Female","Humans","Male","Observer Variation","Parents","Reproducibility of Results"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50721E4B5F14006A5E80923E4AD2D14F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15374416.2014.900719","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":