ck","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Fritz","key":"hengleinpau","last":"Henglein","locid":"d548c40a-f864-4b38-84b8-2acccdc296c1","name":"Henglein, Fritz","orcid":"0000-0001-5190-2125","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tom","key":"hvitvedpau","last":"Hvitved","locid":"df19e452-f56b-401e-aea0-b2c4ecef1479","name":"Hvitved, Tom","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tiziana","key":"margariapedh","last":"Margaria","name":"Margaria, Tiziana","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bernhard","key":"steffenpedh","last":"Steffen","name":"Steffen, Bernhard","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-45234-9_6","eisbn":["9783662452349"],"isbn":["9783662452332"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"73-95","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"6th International Symposium, ISoLA 2014, Imperial, Corfu, Greece, October 8-11, 2014, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Leveraging applications of formal methods, verification and validation. Technologies for mastering change"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84910641672"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","configit a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e3c9b9c0-c072-4dc7-8524-f0cb352ae3a9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Domain-specific languages for enterprise systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-529436","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We study an alternative model of infinitary term rewriting. Instead of a metric on terms, a partial order on partial terms is employed to formalise convergence of reductions. We consider both a weak and a strong notion of convergence and show that the metric model of convergence coincides with the partial order model restricted to total terms. Hence, partial order convergence constitutes a conservative extension of metric convergence, which additionally offers a fine-grained distinction between different levels of divergence. In the second part, we focus our investigation on strong convergence of orthogonal systems. The main result is that the gap between the metric model and the partial order model can be bridged by extending the term rewriting system by additional rules. These extensions are the well-known Böhm extensions. Based on this result, we are able to establish that -- contrary to the metric setting -- orthogonal systems are both infinitarily confluent and infinitarily normalising in the partial order setting. The unique infinitary normal forms that the partial order model admits are Böhm trees.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038409"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["infinitary term rewriting Böhm trees partial order confluence normalisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"partial order infinitary term rewriting","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-10(2:6)2014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038409","identifier":[{"id":"84902001372","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f094aa69-aad5-4aaf-8965-401bcdaaa755","ku-4e9d80db-80c8-44b0-872d-a2f234270675"],"keyword":["infinitary term rewriting, Böhm trees, partial order, confluence, normalisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-489C9F2BA9B4DBDD2E24CE3C15E80E97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-10(2:6)2014","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lmcs-online.org/ojs/viewarticle.php?id=773&layout=abstract","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/125682888/1403.5644.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2168/lmcs-10(2:6)2014","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"2","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","publisher":"International Federation for Computational Logic","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902001372"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f094aa69-aad5-4aaf-8965-401bcdaaa755","ku-4e9d80db-80c8-44b0-872d-a2f234270675"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Partial Order Infinitary Term Rewriting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038409","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A tree transducer is a set of mutually recursive functions transforming an input tree into an output tree. Macro tree transducers extend this recursion scheme by allowing each function to be defined in terms of an arbitrary number of accumulation parameters. In this paper, we show how macro tree transducers can be concisely represented in Haskell, and demonstrate the benefits of utilising such an approach with a number of examples. In particular, tree transducers afford a modular programming style as they can be easily composed and manipulated. Our Haskell representation generalises the original definition of (macro) tree transducers, abolishing a restriction on finite state spaces. However, as we demonstrate, this generalisation does not affect compositionality.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Day, Laurence E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383607"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["tree automaton transducer accumulation composition deforestation Haskell recursion scheme nested recursion polymorphism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"programming macro tree transducers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2502488.2502489","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383607","identifier":[{"id":"84887216048","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a08bc9c8-6e84-4327-837a-23b533866b9b"],"keyword":["tree automaton, transducer, accumulation, composition, deforestation, Haskell, recursion scheme, nested recursion, polymorphism"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-D6432A9335094D99A3A6BBD7AF511812"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2502488.2502489","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurence E.","key":"daypau","last":"Day","name":"Day, Laurence E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2502488.2502489","isbn":["9781450323895"],"pages":"61-72","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th ACM SIGPLAN Workshop on Generic Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887216048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a08bc9c8-6e84-4327-837a-23b533866b9b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Programming macro tree transducers","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383607","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In this extended abstract, we present a simple approach to convergence on term graphs that allows us to unify term graph rewriting and infinitary term rewriting. This approach is based on a partial order and a metric on term graphs. These structures arise as straightforward generalisations of the corresponding structures used in infinitary term rewriting. We compare our simple approach to a more complicated approach that we developed earlier and show that this new approach is superior in many ways. The only unfavourable property that we were able to identify, viz. failure of full correspondence between weak metric and partial order convergence, is rectified by adopting a strong convergence discipline.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384960"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Convergence","Generalisation","Graph Rewriting","Infinitary term rewriting","Metric spaces","Partial order","Strong Convergence","Term Graphs","Term rewriting","Weak convergence"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"convergence in infinitary term graph rewriting systems is simple extended abstract","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384960","ids":["itu-fae067ce-9404-43c6-99c8-a92b47fb3caa"],"keyword":["Convergence","Generalisation","Graph Rewriting","Infinitary Term Rewriting","Metric Spaces","Partial Order","Strong Convergence","Term Graphs","Term Rewriting","Weak Convergence"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-20568B442E4E616AB2619E59F4F403C2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l