{"abstract":"Based on a simple metric and a simple partial order on term graphs, we develop two infinitary calculi of term graph rewriting. We show that, similarly to infinitary term rewriting, the partial order formalisation yields a conservative extension of the metric formalisation of the calculus. By showing that the resulting calculi simulate the corresponding well-established infinitary calculi of term rewriting in a sound and complete manner, we argue for the appropriateness of our approach to capture the notion of infinitary term graph rewriting.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499645"],"event":{"acronym":"FSCD","end":"2012-06-02","place":"Nagoya, jp","start":"2012-05-28","title":"23rd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Simulation","Strong Convergence","Term Graphs","infinitary rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infinitary term graph rewriting is simple sound and complete","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.RTA.2012.69","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-499645","identifier":[{"id":"84880248195","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b1da3943-daf8-438b-87bb-5e1e4071eb4e"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","infinitary rewriting","normalising","simulation","strong convergence","term graphs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-B1187221C4FBB9F1F37CB56DCF50A34A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38429360/bahr12rta_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.RTA.2012.69","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ashish","key":"tiwaripedh","last":"Tiwari","name":"Tiwari, Ashish","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.rta.2012.69","eisbn":["9783939897385"],"issn":["18688969"],"pages":"69-84","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"23rd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications (RTA'12)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880248195"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b1da3943-daf8-438b-87bb-5e1e4071eb4e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infinitary term graph rewriting is simple, sound and complete","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499645","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In previous work we have illustrated the benefits that compositional data types (CDTs) offer for implementing languages and in general for dealing with abstract syntax trees (ASTs). Based on Swierstra's data types \\'a la carte, CDTs are implemented as a Haskell library that enables the definition of recursive data types and functions on them in a modular and extendable fashion. Although CDTs provide a powerful tool for analysing and manipulating ASTs, they lack a convenient representation of variable binders. In this paper we remedy this deficiency by combining the framework of CDTs with Chlipala's parametric higher-order abstract syntax (PHOAS). We show how a generalisation from functors to difunctors enables us to capture PHOAS while still maintaining the features of the original implementation of CDTs, in particular its modularity. Unlike previous approaches, we avoid so-called exotic terms without resorting to abstract types: this is crucial when we want to perform transformations on CDTs that inspect the recursively computed CDTs, e.g. constant folding.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Hvitved, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505367"],"event":{"end":"2012-03-25","place":"Tallinn, ee","start":"2012-03-25","title":"4th Workshop on Mathematically Structured Functional Programming","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parametric compositional data types","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.76.3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505367","identifier":[{"id":"84887187697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bb8bd34a-a0ab-4f15-bd1e-f22a39a1b40d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-D23D3D72018A1821B99E80F6B8040F40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/170135789/Bahr_2012_Paramatric_compositional.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.76.3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tom","key":"hvitvedpau","last":"Hvitved","locid":"df19e452-f56b-401e-aea0-b2c4ecef1479","name":"Hvitved, Tom","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"James","key":"chapmanpedh","last":"Chapman","name":"Chapman, James","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul Blain","key":"levypedh","last":"Levy","name":"Levy, Paul Blain","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.76.3","issn":["20752180"],"pages":"3-24","publisher":"Open Publishing Association","series":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings Fourth Workshop on Mathematically Structured Functional Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887187697"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bb8bd34a-a0ab-4f15-bd1e-f22a39a1b40d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parametric compositional data types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505367","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Tree automata are traditionally used to study properties of tree languages and tree transformations. In this paper, we consider tree automata as the basis for modular and extensible recursion schemes. We show, using well-known techniques, how to derive from standard tree automata highly modular recursion schemes. Functions that are defined in terms of these recursion schemes can be combined, reused and transformed in many ways. This flexibility facilitates the specification of complex transformations in a concise manner, which is illustrated with a number of examples.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518803"],"event":{"acronym":"MPC","end":"2012-06-27","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2012-06-25","title":"11th International Conference on Mathematics of Program Construction","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Compiler","Deforestation","Faculty of Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular tree automata","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38429488/bahr12mpc_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-518803","identifier":[{"id":"84887246741","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d1c3eb64-f1b2-495e-8bd2-ee33443e1594"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","attribute grammar","compiler","deforestation","syntax-directed","tree transducer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-880F39AF481A37A59F7A7E86AF429C1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38429488/bahr12mpc_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeremy","key":"gibbonspedh","last":"Gibbons","name":"Gibbons, Jeremy","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pablo","key":"nogueirapedh","last":"Nogueira","name":"Nogueira, Pablo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-31113-0_14","eisbn":["9783642311130"],"isbn":["9783642311123"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"263-299","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"11th International Conference, MPC 2012, Madrid, Spain, June 25-27, 2012. Proceedings","title":"Mathematics of Program Construction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887246741"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d1c3eb64-f1b2-495e-8bd2-ee33443e1594"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modular tree automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518803","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In previous work we have illustrated the benefits that compositional data types (CDTs) offer for implementing languages and in general for dealing with abstract syntax trees (ASTs). Based on Swierstra's data types à la carte, CDTs are implemented as a Haskell library that enables the definition of recursive data types and functions on them in a modular and extendable fashion. Although CDTs provide a powerful tool for analysing and manipulating ASTs, they lack a convenient representation of variable binders. In this paper we remedy this deficiency by combining the framework of CDTs with Chlipala's parametric higher-order abstract syntax (PHOAS). We show how a generalisation from functors to difunctors enables us to capture PHOAS while still maintaining the features of the original implementation of CDTs, in particular its modularity. Unlike previous approaches, we avoid so-called exotic terms without resorting to abstract types: this is crucial when we want to perform transformations on CDTs that inspect the recursively computed CDTs, e.g. constant folding.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick","Hvitved, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382966"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Abstract Syntax Trees","Compositional Data Types","Haskell","Parametric Higher Order Abstract Syntax","Variable Binders"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parametric compositional data types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84887187697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382966","identifier":[{"id":"84887187697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-72dfbdbc-f7cc-4d48-9723-3cea438c89a3"],"keyword":["Abstract Syntax Trees","Compositional Data Types","Haskell","Parametric Higher-Order Abstract Syntax","Variable Binders"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-D23D3D72018A1821B99E80F6B8040F40"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"hvitvedpau","last":"Hvitved","name":"Hvitved, Tom","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"James","key":"chapmanpedh","last":"Chapman","name":"Chapman, James","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul Blain","key":"levypedh","last":"Levy","name":"Levy, Paul Blain","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.76.3","pages":"3-24","publisher":"Open Publishing Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings Fourth Workshop on Mathematically Structured Functional Programming","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887187697"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-72dfbdbc-f7cc-4d48-9723-3cea438c89a3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parametric Compositional Data Types","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382966","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Based on a simple metric and a simple partial order on term graphs, we develop two infinitary calculi of term graph rewriting. We show that, similarly to infinitary term rewriting, the partial order formalisation yields a conservative extension of the metric formalisation of the calculus. By showing that the resulting calculi simulate the corresponding well-established infinitary calculi of term rewriting in a sound and complete manner, we argue for the appropriateness of our approach to capture the notion of infinitary term graph rewriting.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384640"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Conservative Extension","Infinitary Calculi","Metric Formalisation","Partial order","Term graph rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infinitary term graph rewriting is simple sound and complete","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2012/3485","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384640","identifier":[{"id":"84880248195","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e514c37b-19c0-4585-8bd1-350394457123"],"keyword":["Conservative Extension","Infinitary Calculi","Metric Formalisation","Partial Order","Term Graph Rewriting"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-B1187221C4FBB9F1F37CB56DCF50A34A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2012/3485","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ashish","key":"tiwaripedh","last":"Tiwari","name":"Tiwari, Ashish","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.rta.2012.69","isbn":["9783939897385"],"pages":"69-84","place":"Dagstuhl, Germany","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"23rd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications (RTA'12)","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880248195"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e514c37b-19c0-4585-8bd1-350394457123"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infinitary Term Graph Rewriting is Simple, Sound and Complete","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384640","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Term graph rewriting provides a simple mechanism to finitely represent restricted forms of infinitary term rewriting. The correspondence between infinitary term rewriting and term graph rewriting has been studied to some extent. However, this endeavour is impaired by the lack of an appropriate counterpart of infinitary rewriting on the side of term graphs. We aim to fill this gap by devising two modes of convergence based on a partial order respectively a metric on term graphs. The thus obtained structures generalise corresponding modes of convergence that are usually studied in infinitary term rewriting. We argue that this yields a common framework in which both term rewriting and term graph rewriting can be studied. In order to substantiate our claim, we compare convergence on term graphs and on terms. In particular, we show that the modes of convergence on term graphs are conservative extensions of the corresponding modes of convergence on terms and are preserved under unravelling term graphs to terms. Moreover, we show that many of the properties known from infinitary term rewriting are preserved. This includes the intrinsic completeness of both modes of convergence and the fact that convergence via the partial order is a conservative extension of the metric convergence.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038340"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Completeness","Convergence modes","Faculty of Science","Infinitary term rewriting","Metric","Metric spaces","Partial order","Soundness","Term graph rewriting","Weak convergence","infinitary rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modes of convergence for term graph rewriting","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-8(2:6)2012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038340","identifier":[{"id":"84862701912","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-82d1ce2a-bec4-4c94-b94a-44935998e90b","ku-be42b2a9-6527-40fb-8f81-a98586e84b40"],"keyword":["Convergence modes","Faculty of Science","Infinitary term rewriting","Metric spaces","completeness","infinitary rewriting","metric","partial order","semilattice","soundness","term graph rewriting","weak convergence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F6601FF510CB63DC45BC0AC8BB914D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lmcs-online.org/ojs/viewarticle.php?id=1097","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-8(2:6)2012","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/38429537/bahr12lmcs_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2168/lmcs-8(2:6)2012","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"2","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","publisher":"International Federation for Computational Logic","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84862701912"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-82d1ce2a-bec4-4c94-b94a-44935998e90b","ku-be42b2a9-6527-40fb-8f81-a98586e84b40"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modes of Convergence for Term Graph Rewriting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038340","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Tree automata are traditionally used to study properties of tree languages and tree transformations. In this paper, we consider tree automata as the basis for modular and extensible recursion schemes. We show, using well-known techniques, how to derive from standard tree automata highly modular recursion schemes. Functions that are defined in terms of these recursion schemes can be combined, reused and transformed in many ways. This flexibility facilitates the specification of complex transformations in a concise manner, which is illustrated with a number of examples.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382452"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Functional Reusability","Modular Transformations","Recursion Schemes","Tree Automata","Tree Languages"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular tree automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/ag1626045n91l1w1/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382452","identifier":[{"id":"84887246741","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4f28adee-dd2d-41be-9bfe-9b0504f4a5ab"],"keyword":["Functional Reusability","Modular Transformations","Recursion Schemes","Tree Automata","Tree Languages"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-880F39AF481A37A59F7A7E86AF429C1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.springerlink.com/content/ag1626045n91l1w1/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeremy","key":"gibbonspedh","last":"Gibbons","name":"Gibbons, Jeremy","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pablo","key":"nogueirapedh","last":"Nogueira","name":"Nogueira, Pablo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-31113-0_14","isbn":["9783642311123"],"pages":"263-299","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Mathematics of Program Construction","volume":"7342"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887246741"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4f28adee-dd2d-41be-9bfe-9b0504f4a5ab"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modular Tree Automata","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382452","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In this dissertation we investigate two independent areas of research. In the first part, we develop techniques for implementing programming languages in a modular fashion. Within this problem domain, we focus on operations on typed abstract syntax trees with the goal of developing a framework that facilitates the definition, manipulation and composition of such operations. The result of our work is a comprehensive combinator library that provides these facilities. What sets our approach apart is the use of recursion schemes derived from tree automata in order to implement operations on abstract syntax trees. The second part is concerned with infinitary rewriting, a field that studies transfinite rewrite sequences. We extend the established theory of infinitary rewriting in two ways: (1) a novel approach to convergence in infinitary rewriting that replaces convergence in a metric space with the limit inferior in a partially ordered set; (2) extending infinitary term rewriting to infinitary term graph rewriting.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504440"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular implementation of programming languages and a partial order approach to infinitary rewriting","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-504440","ids":["ku-b9f78d6d-29a2-4948-8cd1-1a1f3f5d1227"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D56DAB1D09B7F5D8FEDF38AB782F7021"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"466","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b9f78d6d-29a2-4948-8cd1-1a1f3f5d1227"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modular Implementation of Programming Languages and a Partial-Order Approach to Infinitary Rewriting","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-504440","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Term graph rewriting provides a simple mechanism to finitely represent restricted forms of infinitary term rewriting. The correspondence between infinitary term rewriting and term graph rewriting has been studied to some extent. However, this endeavour is impaired by the lack of an appropriate counterpart of infinitary rewriting on the side of term graphs. We aim to fill this gap by devising two modes of convergence based on a partial order resp. a metric on term graphs. The thus obtained structures generalise corresponding modes of convergence that are usually studied in infinitary term rewriting. We argue that this yields a common framework in which both term rewriting and term graph rewriting can be studied. In order to substantiate our claim, we compare convergence on term graphs and on terms. In particular, we show that the resulting infinitary calculi of term graph rewriting exhibit the same correspondence as we know it from term rewriting: Convergence via the partial order is a conservative extension of the metric convergence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383460"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["term graphs partial order metric infinitary rewriting graph rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modes of convergence for term graph rewriting","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2011/3113","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383460","identifier":[{"id":"84880191353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9572c41d-add7-4ab8-9887-3864f622a8da"],"keyword":["term graphs, partial order, metric, infinitary rewriting, graph rewriting"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-B091E884B8DD3EC6A0ACF322D5F6F2B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2011/3113","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"schmidtschaupedh","last":"Schmidt-Schau","name":"Schmidt-Schau, Manfred","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.rta.2011.139","isbn":["9783939897309"],"pages":"139-154","place":"Dagstuhl, Germany","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"22nd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications (RTA'11)","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880191353"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9572c41d-add7-4ab8-9887-3864f622a8da"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modes of Convergence for Term Graph Rewriting","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383460","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Cyclic term graph rewriting has been shown to be adequate for simulating certain forms of infinitary term rewriting. These forms are, however, quite restrictive and it would be beneficial to lift these restriction at least for a limited class of rewriting systems. In order to better understand the correspondences between infinite reduction sequences over terms and finite reductions over cyclic term graphs, we explore different variants of infinitary term graph rewriting calculi. To this end, we study different modes of convergence for term graph rewriting that generalise the modes of convergence usually considered in infinitary term rewriting. After discussing several different alternatives, we identify a complete semilattice on term graphs and derive from it a complete metric space on term graphs. Equipped with these structures, we can -- analogously to the term rewriting case -- define both a metric and a partial order model of infinitary term graph rewriting. The resulting calculi of infinitary term graph rewriting reveal properties similar to the corresponding infinitary term rewriting calculi.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524642"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-02","place":"Saarbrücken, de","start":"2011-04-02","title":"6th International Workshop on Computing with Terms and Graphs","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Term graph rewriting","Term rewriting","infinitary rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from infinitary term rewriting to cyclic term graph rewriting and back","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.48","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524642","ids":["ku-dbae4dff-6fd2-4e29-bd62-163a4e18dd0a"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","infinitary rewriting","term graph rewriting","term rewriting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3B7CC33A2414F5912907259D75B176BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.48","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/34445062/abstract.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rachid","key":"echahedpedh","last":"Echahed","name":"Echahed, Rachid","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.48","issn":["20752180"],"pages":"2","series":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 6th International Workshop on Computing with Terms and Graphs"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dbae4dff-6fd2-4e29-bd62-163a4e18dd0a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From infinitary term rewriting to cyclic term graph rewriting and back","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524642","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"We describe how to perform monadic computations over recursive data structures with fine grained control over the evaluation strategy. This solves the issue that the definition of a recursive monadic function already determines the evaluation strategy due to the necessary sequencing of the monadic operations. We show that compositional data types already provide the structure needed in order to delay monadic computations at any point of the computation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384947"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["monads tree transformations evaluation strategies Haskell generic programming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation à la carte non strict evaluation via compositional data types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mrtc.mdh.se/nwpt2011/index.php?choice=program","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384947","ids":["itu-f9c7e521-c823-422e-8eb9-868d2f09448d"],"keyword":["monads,tree transformations,evaluation strategies,Haskell,generic programming"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A6DDE287150B653EF12DB33C725BE8D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mrtc.mdh.se/nwpt2011/index.php?choice=program","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"5e271e6a-7a91-47bd-9f12-3b73f4e0d7ac","name":"Bahr, Patrick","orcid":"0000-0003-1600-8261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"petterssonpedh","last":"Pettersson","name":"Pettersson, Paul","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristina","key":"seceleanupedh","last":"Seceleanu","name":"Seceleanu, Cristina","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"38-40","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 23rd Nordic Workshop on Programming Theory"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f9c7e521-c823-422e-8eb9-868d2f09448d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluation à la Carte: Non-Strict Evaluation via Compositional Data Types","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384947","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Term graph rewriting provides a simple mechanism to finitely represent restricted forms of infinitary term rewriting. The correspondence between infinitary term rewriting and term graph rewriting has been studied to some extent. However, this endeavour is impaired by the lack of an appropriate counterpart of infinitary rewriting on the side of term graphs. We aim to fill this gap by devising two modes of convergence based on a partial order resp. a metric on term graphs. The thus obtained structures generalise corresponding modes of convergence that are usually studied in infinitary term rewriting. We argue that this yields a common framework in which both term rewriting and term graph rewriting can be studied. In order to substantiate our claim, we compare convergence on term graphs and on terms. In particular, we show that the resulting infinitary calculi of term graph rewriting exhibit the same correspondence as we know it from term rewriting: Convergence via the partial order is a conservative extension of the metric convergence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bahr, Patrick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461409"],"event":{"end":"2011-06-01","place":"Novi Sad, rs","start":"2011-05-30","title":"22nd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Graph Rewriting","Metric","Partial order","Term Graphs","infinitary rewriting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modes of convergence for term graph rewriting","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.RTA.2011.139","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461409","identifier":[{"id":"84880191353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-71b9c7c0-48ac-4ab2-879b-ba77cfcf0c54"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","graph rewriting","infinitary rewriting","metric","partial order","term graphs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-B091E884B8DD3EC6A0ACF322D5F6F2B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.RTA.2011.139","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/33638090/bahr11rta_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Patrick","key":"bahrpau","last":"Bahr","locid":"0df28789-7837-4997-9abf-945875a7c0c9","name":"Bahr, Patrick","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"schmidtschaußpedh","last":"Schmidt-Schauß","name":"Schmidt-Schauß, Manfred","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.rta.2011.139","eisbn":["9783939897309"],"issn":["18688969"],"pages":"139-154","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"22nd International Conference on Rewriting Techniques and Applications (RTA'11)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880191353"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-71b9c7c0-48ac-4ab2-879b-ba77cfcf0c